00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:42.450
So the crime fraud exception is a legal principle
which allows certain confidential communications,

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:47.599
like, for example, those between an attorney
and their client to be disclosed in court.

00:02:47.599 --> 00:02:52.680
If they were made to further the commission
of a crime or a fraud.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:59.621
So if you use your attorney client relationship
to plan or carry out a crime or fraud, then

00:02:59.621 --> 00:03:02.280
it's not protected by attorney client privilege.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:04.530
It's actually a really simple legal principle.

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:09.690
So if you have a lawyer and you consult with
your lawyer to commit a fraud, to cover up

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:13.700
a crime or whatever, those conversations,
those communications could be subject to the

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:15.010
crime fraud exception.

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:17.730
They aren't protected by attorney client privilege.

